{"_v":1,"id":"dinner-at-eight-2002","bd":{"positive":0,"mixed":1,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Ben Brantley","o":"The New York Times","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"http://theater.nytimes.com/mem/theater/treview.html?html_title=&amp;tols_title=DINNER%20AT%20EIGHT%20(PLAY)&amp;byline=By%20BEN%20BRANTLEY&amp;pdate=20021220&amp;id=1077011429752","d":"2002-12-20","q":"If you plan to spend time on a sinking ship, it might as well be the Titanic. The main characters in George S. Kaufman and Edna Ferber’s ”Dinner at Eight,” which has been given a sumptuous shop window of a revival by Theater, are headed straight for icebergs in their lives. It is, after all, the height of the Depression, and fortunes tumble daily."}],"au":{"score":70,"designation":"Shrugging","sources":{"mz":{"s":70,"c":1,"sr":3.5}}},"pd":"2002-11-23","ca":[{"n":"Joanne Camp","r":"Lucy Talbot"},{"n":"Rhys Coiro","r":"Eddie"},{"n":"Kevin Conway","r":"Dan Packard"},{"n":"John Dossett","r":"Dr. J. Wayne Talbot"},{"n":"Christine Ebersole","r":"Millicent Jordan"},{"n":"Julian Gamble","r":"Musician"},{"n":"Enid Graham","r":"Dora"},{"n":"Joe Grifasi","r":"Max Kane"},{"n":"Byron Jennings","r":"Larry Renault"},{"n":"Simon Jutras","r":"Gustave"},{"n":"Joseph Kamal","r":"Musician"},{"n":"Karl Kenzler","r":"Mr. Hatfield"},{"n":"Mark La Mura","r":"Musician"},{"n":"Anne Lange","r":"Miss Alden"},{"n":"Philip LeStrange","r":"The Waiter"},{"n":"Mark Lotito","r":"Ricci"},{"n":"Charlotte Maier","r":"Tina"},{"n":"Peter Maloney","r":"Joe Stengel"},{"n":"Deborah Mayo","r":"Miss Copeland"},{"n":"Ann McDonough","r":"Hattie Loomis"},{"n":"James Rebhorn","r":"Oliver Jordan"},{"n":"Brian Reddy","r":"Ed Loomis"},{"n":"Marian Seldes","r":"Carlotta Vance"},{"n":"Sloane Shelton","r":"Mrs. Wendel"},{"n":"Emily Skinner","r":"Kitty Packard"},{"n":"Samantha Soule","r":"Paula Jordan"},{"n":"David Wohl","r":"Mr. Fitch"}]}